   "evidence": "OrthogonalSpanning.lean:106-110: after `have h := hv _ (g.reflection_isPairStabilizer ...)` the remaining four lines (`rw [reflection_apply, sub_eq_self, smul_eq_zero] at h; rcases h with h | h; simpa [h2, hu] using h; simp [h] at hu`) use only `hu` and `h2` \u2014 `a`, `b` and `IsPairStabilizer` play no part. Reflection.lean:69 `reflection_apply_of_orthogonal (h : g u v = 0) : reflection g u v = v` is exactly the other direction and is left incomplete.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Mathematics/LinearAlgebra/BilinearForm/OrthogonalSpanning.lean",
   "fix": "Add to Reflection.lean, beside `reflection_apply_of_orthogonal`, `lemma reflection_apply_eq_self_iff (g : BilinForm K V) (h2 : (2 : K) \u2260 0) {u : V} (hu : g u u \u2260 0) (v : V) : g.reflection u v = v \u2194 g u v = 0` (the `\u2190` direction is `reflection_apply_of_orthogonal`), and reduce `apply_eq_zero_of_forall_isPairStabilizer` to applying `hv` at `g.reflection_isPairStabilizer` and rewriting with it.",
   "issue": "`apply_eq_zero_of_forall_isPairStabilizer` instantiates its `\u2200 f, IsPairStabilizer a b f \u2192 f v = v` hypothesis at one element and then proves, inline at lines 107-110, the general fact `g.reflection u v = v \u2192 g u v = 0` (for `g u u \u2260 0`, `2 \u2260 0`). That fact needs no pair, no `a`/`b` and no stabilizer, and is the missing converse of `reflection_apply_of_orthogonal` (Reflection.lean:69); as written no other caller can reach it without constructing a full pair stabilizer.",
   "line": 103
  }
